{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","cve_id":"CVE-2026-115570","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","summary":"Electron: Mitigation for compromised eMudhra intermediate certificates","description":"### Impact\n\nA set of eMudhra intermediate certificates were compromised and are being blocked by browsers and other TLS clients. This Electron update adds the same block to both Chromium networking and Node.js `tls`, `https` and `fetch`. On earlier versions, an attacker holding a certificate issued through these intermediates and able to intercept network traffic could impersonate a TLS server to an app.\n\nApps are only affected if they make TLS connections over a network an attacker can intercept. Apps that make no network connections are not affected.\n\nOther software has shipped the same mitigation, including Go (CVE-2026-111943) and Firefox (CVE-2026-113470).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nThere are no app side workarounds, you must update to a patched version of Electron.\n\n### Fixed Versions\n\n* `45.0.0-beta.6`\n* `44.9.1`\n* `43.8.1`\n* `42.11.16`\n\n### For more information\n\nIf you have any questions or comments about this advisory, email us at [security@electronjs.org](mailto:security@electronjs.org)","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/electron/electron/security-advisories/GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","source_code_location":"https://github.com/electron/electron","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-115570","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/electron/electron/security/advisories/GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9","https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/55127","https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/55128","https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/55129","https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/55130","https://github.com/electron/electron/commit/093583c71be71c85453e6e225137bf2af755fbcc","https://github.com/electron/electron/commit/1d2f13b1985444a38abf389db38228ac42f5bcad","https://github.com/electron/electron/commit/817c43f925677eb88034bfba4f0b8dfd28e7ad20","https://github.com/electron/electron/commit/e02265be96c5e13ae43644ef482b718e1e800499","https://github.com/electron/electron/releases/tag/v42.11.16","https://github.com/electron/electron/releases/tag/v43.8.1","https://github.com/electron/electron/releases/tag/v44.9.1","https://github.com/electron/electron/releases/tag/v45.0.0-beta.6","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-jr5w-w6x2-84p9"],"published_at":"2026-10-23T20:53:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T20:53:43Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-10-23T20:53:41Z","nvd_published_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"electron"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 45.0.0-alpha.1, < 45.0.0-beta.6","first_patched_version":"45.0.0-beta.6","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"electron"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 44.0.0-alpha.1, < 44.9.1","first_patched_version":"44.9.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"electron"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 43.0.0-alpha.1, < 43.8.1","first_patched_version":"43.8.1","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"electron"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 42.11.16","first_patched_version":"42.11.16","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N","score":7.4},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":0.0}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-299","name":"Improper Check for Certificate Revocation"}],"credits":[{"user":{"login":"MarshallOfSound","id":6634592,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2MzQ1OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6634592?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarshallOfSound","html_url":"https://github.com/MarshallOfSound","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarshallOfSound/followers","foll